# SocratiCode semantic-index exclusions (gitignore syntax; layered on
# SocratiCode's built-in defaults + .gitignore). See usa-wa#143.
#
# Vendored skill trees are third-party docs, not this repo's code. Indexing
# them inflates embedding time and lets vendored content outrank our own code
# in codebase_search. skills/ needs no entry of its own: since #263 every one
# of its entries is a symlink into the already-excluded skills-vendor/ (there
# are no local overrides left), and the indexer does not follow them — no
# skills/ path appears in the code index. Re-check that if an override is
# ever added back.
skills-vendor/
.claude/skills/

# Dated prose. All three are declared *directory* context artifacts, so they
# stay fully reachable through codebase_context_search — excluding them here
# only stops them competing with first-party source in codebase_search, where
# a superseded plan outranks the code that replaced it. ~1.1 MB of ~6.7 MB
# indexable bytes. Asked and answered in the #406 init-socraticode re-run;
# the reverse call (exclude a directory that is NOT an artifact) would make it
# unsearchable, which is why this one is keyed to their artifact status.
docs/plans/
docs/specs/
docs/research/
